REA — Recreate Extractable Field → Auto-Fill
Recreate the Extractable Field feature from scratch; do not revert commits or restore the old implementation.
First inspect the existing template parameter/configuration, persistence, rendering and auto-fill architecture.
An existing required template field can be marked Extractable. For example:
{reference_number}
receives:
MP260831.1923.T7382831
In the Admin Dashboard, the admin provides an example input and defines extractable substrings using square brackets:
MP[260831].[1923].T7382831
REA must detect 260831 and 1923 as separate extracted values.
The admin must then be able to map each extracted value to an existing template field, for example:
[260831] → {date}
[1923]   → {time}
Finally, each mapping may have an optional transformation/modification step before the value is assigned to the target field. For example:
260831 → transform YYMMDD → 2026-08-31 → {date}
1923   → transform HHmm → 19:23 → {time}
Keep these concerns separate:
Source field → Extraction → Mapping → Transformation → Target field
The agent should only enter the normal source value:
MP260831.1923.T7382831
and REA should perform the configured extraction, transformation and auto-fill automatically.
Build a clear Admin UI for these three stages: Define Extraction → Map Extracted Values → Configure Transformation, with live previews where practical.
Preserve multi-tenancy, existing template functionality, ordinary agent profile behavior and existing authorization. Do not add PIN requirements to normal agents.
Add tests for extraction, multiple substrings, mapping, date/time transformations, persistence, and runtime auto-fill.
Do not rewrite unrelated functionality. Inspect the current architecture first, then implement this feature cleanly around the existing template system.